# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# Two warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 28 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, each with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with `{}'." Every hit is a
#       closing delimiter that legitimately carries a script: the module
#       $(\FqG)^{\ell}$ and $(\FqG)^{k \times \ell}$, the sequence
#       $(C_{\ell})_{\ell}$, and the group $(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})^{n}$ and
#       its relatives, where the exponent is the number of factors.  (7 hits)
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each hit is the
#       final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the source paper or
#       from the follow-up cited in Remark~\ref{rem:progress}. The punctuation
#       belongs to the quoted text; moving it out would misquote.  (5 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on; the one warning 13 hit chktex raised on the
# first draft ("HQC." at the end of a sentence) was fixed with \@ rather
# than silenced. As of 28 August 2026 the file is clean under this config
# and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n38
}
